Hi gang,

After an otherwise unnecessary degree of abdication procrostination on my
part, Boas Betzler <BOAS@de.ibm.com> has now taken over responsibility for
the PowerPC Embedded HOWTO. The choice of new maintainer was somewhat
arbitrary, as I had a remarkably large number of quality applicants for the
role of assuming maintainership -- I did mention that it was an entirely
volunteer position, didn't I? :-). Boas is actively working in embedded
Linux full time, has a long history of Linux involvement and should do a
good job.

A very big Thank You to everyone who expressed interest in this role.
Although I will no longer be actively involved in the HOWTO, I recommend
that everyone interested in contributing contact Boas via E-mail, so that
he can co-ordinate future additions and act as a clearing-house for
updates. Alternatively, pick any aspect of embedded Linux development for
which you can't find adequate documentation, write a new HOWTO to cover it,
and submit to the Linux Documentation Project. Good luck with your
projects!

See you around,
Graham

